The changes in these diffs are related to handling `MetadataAttribute.SCORE`. The logic is correct but can be improved for clarity and maintainability.
In `#YJM1Z`, the loop can be simplified by removing unnecessary variables and conditions:
```java
var outputIterator = plan.output().iterator();
var isTimeSeries = plan.indexMode() == IndexMode.TIME_SERIES;
Attribute tsid = null, timestamp = null, score = null;
while (outputIterator.hasNext()) {
    Attribute attr = outputIterator.next();
    if (attr instanceof MetadataAttribute ma) {
        if (ma.name().equals(MetadataAttribute.SCORE)) {
            score = attr;
        } else if (isTimeSeries && ma.name().equals(MetadataAttribute.TSID_FIELD)) {
            tsid = attr;
        } else if (isTimeSeries && ma.name().equals(MetadataAttribute.TIMESTAMP_FIELD)) {
            timestamp = attr;
        }
    }
    if (score != null && (!isTimeSeries || (tsid != null && timestamp != null))) {
        break;
    }
}
if (isTimeSeries && (tsid == null || timestamp == null)) {
    throw new IllegalStateException("_tsid or @timestamp are missing from the time-series source");
}
attributes.add(docId);
if (score != null) {
    attributes.add(score);
}
if (isTimeSeries) {
    attributes.add(tsid);
    attributes.add(timestamp);
}
```
In `#6A7RH`, the method `hasScoring` is correctly implemented but can be optimized by using a more efficient stream operation:
```java
public boolean hasScoring() {
    return attrs().stream().anyMatch(a -> MetadataAttribute.SCORE.equals(a.name()));
}
```

